  "goodToKnow": "Die Herzogin is a duchess; der Herzog a duke, and das Herzogtum a duchy, such as the historic Herzogtum Bayern or Württemberg. The word originally meant army leader (Heer + ziehen). Since the Weimar Constitution of 1919, German nobility has no legal privileges, and titles are simply part of the surname. Herzogin Anna Amalia of Saxe-Weimar made Weimar a cultural centre; her library is a UNESCO site. Plural: die Herzoginnen."
